    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32419" root="غمز" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَامِزٌ</span></b>  [meaning <i>Limping,</i> or <i>halting,</i> &amp;c., and
<i>having a limping,</i> or <i>halting,</i> &amp;c.,] is like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظَالِعٌ</span>:
sometimes used as a possessive noun; and [therefore] one does not say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَامِزَةٌ</span>. (O and TA in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظلع</span>.)

